From: Erfan Abdi <erfangplus@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] apklayer compat: RELR types for glibc before 2.36

glibc before 2.36 (Ubuntu 22.04: 2.35, Sailfish OS 5.0: 2.30) has no RELR types in elf.h; the linker uses them (Android's libraries are
linked with --pack-dyn-relocs=android+relr). A patch, not a forced -include: a subproject's c_args from default_options apply only from
Meson 1.8 on. Applied by meson.build only when elf.h lacks Elf64_Relr.
---
diff --git a/linker/linker.h b/linker/linker.h
--- a/linker/linker.h
+++ b/linker/linker.h
@@ -30,6 +30,13 @@
 #define _LINKER_H_

 #include <elf.h>
+#ifndef DT_RELR
+typedef Elf32_Word Elf32_Relr;
+typedef Elf64_Xword Elf64_Relr;
+#define DT_RELRSZ 35
+#define DT_RELR 36
+#define DT_RELRENT 37
+#endif
 #include <link.h>
 #include <stdbool.h>
 #include <sys/types.h>
